## Axis B — #86 schematic numbers centered

Fix: `src/ui/Schematic.tsx` — non-band label x `m.x` → `m.x + layout.pitch/2`
(:307); band significant label x `xOf(index)` → `xOf(index) + pitch/2` (:215).
Boundary TICKS unchanged (line x1/x2 still at `xOf(index)` / `m.x`).
Tests: `src/ui/smoke.test.tsx` › Schematic ›
  (i)  "centers non-band machine labels under the cell (m.x + pitch/2) (#86)"
  (ii) "band mode: label centers at xOf + pitch/2 while the tick stays at xOf (#86)"

- PASS: fix in → `Tests  2 passed`. All S15 layout thinning pins (nine-pair
  residual, labeled subsets, ticks>labels) still green (`layout.test.ts` +
  smoke #78 pin) — the +pitch/2 shift is constant, so label-to-label distances
  are unchanged.
- BREAK: reverted BOTH x expressions back to `m.x` / `xOf(index)`; both pins
  FAILED:
  > (i)  `expected '…' to contain '<text class="machine-label" x="46.5" y="'`
  >      (broken markup rendered the label at bare `x="24"` — the cell's left
  >      edge / boundary, N=20 pitch=45 so center is 24+22.5=46.5)
  > (ii) `expected '…' to contain '<text class="machine-label" x="36" y="'`
  >      (broken markup rendered the first band label at bare `x="32"` — on its
  >      boundary tick; band pitch=8 so center is 32+4=36, and the tick line
  >      `x1="32" x2="32"` stays put either way, proving tick ≠ label)
- RESTORE: fix back → `Tests  2 passed`.

The break exactly reproduces Michael's report ("numbers arent in the middle …
hard to see where the feed out is") — labels sitting ON the boundary line.
